    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Description\n\nUnsure whether this feature is in the  scope of the Mini project, but I wanted it so I implemented it. I made it optional by adding a config boolean which defaults to false.  With the config boolean true, after typing `<Space>` (my `<leader>` key) followed by `<BS>` I see the following -- which reflects my particular nvim config:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/846909f6-e111-40a7-81af-41692c64310c)\n\nTyping `<BS>` or `<ESC>` at this window closes it.",
